# Accessibility Implementation Rules

<rule>
name: atlas_accessibility
description: Standards for implementing proper accessibility features
filters:
  - type: file_extension
    pattern: "\\.(?:jsx|tsx|html)$"
  - type: content
    pattern: "(?i)accessibility|a11y|aria|screen reader"

actions:
  - type: suggest
    message: |
      When implementing accessibility features:

      ## Semantic HTML
      - Use HTML5 semantic elements (<header>, <nav>, <main>, etc.)
      - Maintain correct heading hierarchy (h1-h6)
      - Add appropriate ARIA roles when HTML semantics are insufficient
      - Implement document landmarks (banner, navigation, main, etc.)
      - Ensure all form controls have associated labels

      ## Keyboard Navigation
      - Manage focus order and states logically
      - Ensure all interactive elements are keyboard accessible
      - Provide keyboard shortcuts for complex interactions
      - Make focus indicators clearly visible
      - Include skip links for bypassing repetitive content

      ## Screen Reader Support
      - Use descriptive ARIA attributes (aria-label, aria-expanded, etc.)
      - Provide meaningful alt text for images
      - Implement live regions for dynamic content updates
      - Include descriptions for complex widgets
      - Announce critical state changes to assistive technology

      ## Visual Accessibility
      - Maintain WCAG AA contrast ratio (4.5:1 for normal text)
      - Support text scaling up to 200% without loss of content
      - Design responsively for various devices and zoom levels
      - Respect prefers-reduced-motion media query
      - Design distinct focus and hover states

      ## Testing & Compliance
      - Test with screen readers (NVDA, VoiceOver, JAWS)
      - Follow WCAG 2.1 AA standards
      - Conduct testing with actual users with disabilities
      - Use automated tools (axe, Lighthouse) for initial checks
      - Document accessibility features and known issues

examples:
  - input: "Adding a new form component"
    output: "Form includes labeled controls, appropriate ARIA attributes, and complete keyboard support"

metadata:
  priority: high
  version: 1.0
</rule> 